{{- /*
The account-wide deny rules Antigravity's CLI reads, merged into
~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json.

The CLI only. The IDE ships the same rule syntax and reads none of this file:
the keys beside these are the CLI's own, and the IDE's permission scopes are
its own state. See the antigravity target in internal/install/agents.go.

GENERATED. The paths come from internal/install/protectedpaths.go, written
once and rendered into each agent's own spelling; nothing here is a path of its
own. Add one there.

Deny rules only. The documented precedence is deny over ask over allow, so
these hold against an operator's own allow rather than losing to it, and there
is no default this is entitled to replace.

read_file and write_file take the same list. A value the agent cannot read is
one it can still destroy, and an age key replaced is every managed file
unreadable retroactively.
*/ -}}
{
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
{{ jsonLines "      " (agyRules .Layout) }}
    ]
  }
}
